"""Layer 1 MLP down-projection, component 5899: a document-start feature.

What it does: the component is silent except at the first token of each document. The
model restarts its position count at every document boundary, and at that first token the
component writes a token-specific value into the residual stream (its value depends only on
that token, since the token has no earlier context). Elsewhere it is about zero.

The value at a document start, read from the token's text:
  - a function word with a leading space (" to", " a", " the", " of") is slightly negative;
  - a blank token is negative;
  - a digit, or a Unicode symbol with a leading space, is about 2.5 to 2.8;
  - a symbol or code opener with no leading space ("/*", "#!", "**", "#include", "<?") is
    large (8);
  - prose punctuation (",", ".", ":", ")") is about 1;
  - a single capital letter ("G", "M", "Q") or a newline or tab is about 6;
  - a word piece with no leading space and a lowercase start ("fr", "contin") is about 5;
  - an ordinary word with a leading space is about 2.6 to 2.9; a capitalised word is about 2.5;
  - other text (non-Latin letters, mixed tokens) is about 3 to 4.

Limits: this is a coarse, readable approximation. A full per-token table of the same
values reproduces nearly all the variance; these character classes capture part of it.
The rare exceptions (a run of 512 repeated middle dots, a few positions just after a
document start) are not modelled.
"""

import re
import unicodedata

READS = ()

FUNCTION_WORDS = set(
    "the a an of to in and is for that with on be by as are was at from this or not it "
    "he she they we you i his her its their our your than then but if so do does did has "
    "have had which who what when where while into over under about after before can will "
    "would should could may might also just more most very all any each other some such "
    "only there here".split()
)
PROSE_PUNCTUATION = set(",.:;)]\"'!?")


def doc_start_value(token: str) -> float:
    core = token.lstrip(" ")
    space = token.startswith(" ")
    if core == "":
        return -1.0
    if space and core in FUNCTION_WORDS:
        return -0.5
    if re.fullmatch(r"[0-9]+", core):
        return 2.8
    if re.fullmatch(r"\s+", core) and "\n" in core or core == "\t":
        return 6.0
    if all(unicodedata.category(c)[0] in "PS" for c in core):
        if space:
            return 2.5
        if core in PROSE_PUNCTUATION:
            return 1.0
        return 8.0 if re.match(r"[/*#<`\\_\[{]", core) else 4.5
    if re.fullmatch(r"[A-Za-z]+", core):
        if space:
            return 2.9 if core[0].islower() else 2.6
        if len(core) == 1:
            return 6.0
        if core.isupper():
            return 4.4
        return 4.9 if core[0].islower() else 2.5
    return 4.0 if not space else 3.0


def step(carry, prefix, upstream):
    new_document = prefix.position == 0 or prefix.document_ids[-1] != prefix.document_ids[-2]
    if not new_document:
        return carry, 0.0
    return carry, doc_start_value(prefix.token_strings[-1])

