"""Negative pulses for 直 and related spellings, plus selected r-cluster stems.

The strongest rules recognize the Han character 直 (straight/direct), common
compounds, Vietnamese trực and Korean 직. A second family recognizes Russian
прям-/напря-/прост-, Czech/Slovak pří-/prí-/prů-, and some other pr spellings.
These are lexical rules, not a claim that all these words share one meaning.
Pulses depend on whether a spelling is split between tokens. All other
positions predict zero; small, diffuse activations are deliberately omitted.
