Predict a positive activation for a single-space token after a space/tab
block, especially in indentation. Predict a negative activation after real
or escaped newlines and apparent string-opening quotes. Earlier spacing
conventions adjust the strength: count single spaces followed by another
space, and single spaces followed by numbers. Repeated tabs respond more
weakly. Initial whitespace effects are amplified; other tokens predict zero.

These formatting rules omit token-specific lexical responses, including
those on ordinary text at document starts.
