"""A formatting response, strongest before ordinary text has begun.

Space indentation is strongly negative at a document's start; the final
single-space piece of a split indentation run is positive later on.
Initial punctuation and zero have smaller special responses. Repeating an
initial formatting token preserves its initial response (notably dot leaders).
Other token-specific lexical effects are deliberately left near zero.
