"""Layer-1 MLP component 5935: the "et" of a citation or a Latin/English "et".

It fires on the word "et" in English, Latin or scientific text. Strongest is "et"
right after a capitalized author name, as in "(Fisher et al., 2007)" or "Schweder
et al.", where the next word is almost always "al". Latin "et cetera" and English
"et" in similar text also respond. The French conjunction "et" ("and") stays low,
as do other short pieces spelled e-t (ret, eth, ety, Cyrillic ет/эт) at a weaker
level. Whole English words that merely contain "et" (get, let, set, return) stay
near zero, and so does almost everything else. The prediction reads only the
current token and a short window of the text before it.
