"""layers.1.mlp.down_proj:5945, predicted from the text itself.

This component is nearly silent (typical size 0.05) and speaks in rare, large bursts.
Its largest negative bursts sit on the word "of" in a page count: the "of" of a page
footer such as "Page 3 of 12" (about -6.4). A step or part count gives a weaker
negative ("Step 2 of 6", about -3), and any other "3 of ..." a faint one (about -0.4).
It also goes negative (about -2.5) on a backtick that opens a code span at the start
of a line, usually the line after a markdown heading. Its positive bursts sit on web
boilerplate: "permalink" (forum anchors, about +1.6), "posted" at the start of a line
(about +1.4), and "This code is contributed by" (about +3).

